/*
containerUser
-------------

Defines the Linux user that **all** processes inside the container run as.

• If omitted, the container starts as `root` or as the last `USER` specified
  in your Dockerfile.
• Need the IDE backend or its tools to run as a different user?
  Use **remoteUser** instead.

⚠️  The user must already exist in the image and have the right permissions.
    Add one in your Dockerfile, for example:

      RUN useradd -m devuser && \
          chown -R devuser /workspace
*/
{
  "name": "1_6-spec_containerUser",
  "build": {
    "dockerfile": "./Dockerfile"
  },
  "containerUser": "root"
}

